       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1000 mg is five times the maximum recommended sertraline dose for adults, which is 200 mg/day. At that dose the patient would be at serious risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and arrhythmia. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function, no allergies) would justify it.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **100 mg once daily**, which is a common maintenance dose. Typical dosing is 50\u2013200 mg daily.\n- **50 mg once daily**, which is the usual starting dose for depression, and for many anxiety indications 25 mg is the usual start.\n- **200 mg once daily**, which is the maximum dose.\n\nTell me the dose you intended and I'll enter it right away. If 1000 mg is truly what you want, for example as part of a protocol I don't know about, please confirm that explicitly. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy before it's entered."
